  "title": "When the least bond size grows with depth",
  "subject": "Bond size and depth in nested patterns",
  "conclusion": "If a fixed run of unobserved levels on a recursive branch allows every possible incoming tuple to combine with every possible outgoing tuple, every finite bond from the top to a fresh distinction at depth s has at least 1 + ceil(s/r) members, where r is the run length. A compatible cycle of three-member bonds and carried distinctions gives a bond of at most s + 3 members at every positive depth.",
